==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Frosty Kai, type μ''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Frostspirit Kai, type μ''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
In the same way that her normal counterpart is the premier shield against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|floating]] enemies, Frosty Kai is decently tanky against [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] and [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]]. Able to soak up damage from them like no other, Frosty Kai can free up meatshield slots in your lineup in stages dominated by aliens or angels, as well as cluster them together to take them out all at once. Use her alongside units with a Massive Damage effect (such as [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]] for aliens or [[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Kalisa]] for Angels), to create a combination of an unstoppable force and an immovable object that will shred everything in your path.

Of course, Frosty Kai will likely get shredded late game due to below-average HP for a tank, so much of her value lies in earlier stages where the health is high enough. However, she still falls off quite dramatically. Combined with a lack of status immunities for both traits she has to face, usage beyond later SOL stages requires her true form.

=== '''True Form''' ===
In the simplest of terms, Frostspirit Kai type μ is no longer likely to get shredded anymore, all thanks to her incredibly high health bar that feels in line with her original variant. Since her health is doubled, she now tanks to a satisfying degree. To top it off, her health is so high that she can tank in mixed stages, and she even has especially high speed, which shows that Frostspirit Kai is ideal for tanking at any point in the game.

Do note that Frostspirit Kai still lacks immunities. It's not a dealbreaker, but it is noticeable in stages with enemies that use status effects or [[Surge Attack|Surge]]/[[Wave Attack|Wave]]/[[Explosion]], such as [[Ange Lackey]]. Luckily, that's pretty much her only major issue, and her stats are more than enough for her job.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Freeze]]''' works under the assumption that Frostspirit Kai actually hits anything worth Freezing. Unfortunately, she is highly prone to getting distracted by peons and usually never gets the opportunity to properly align on a desired enemy. Its uptime is fairly decent (~46%) all things considered, so the biggest limiting factor is its practicality at the end of the day.

'''[[Barrier Breaker]]''' is situational, and suffers from much of the same problems as her Freeze. She fares a little better though, since her main targets for Barrier Breaking are usually going to be [[Youcan]] and [[UltraBaaBaa]], both of whom you'll have no trouble keeping in place while Kai finishes her attack animation. However, Frostspirit Kai isn't special in this regard, and any other readily available Barrier Breaker usually gets the job done just as well.

Finally, '''[[Immune to Warp]]''' is an ability Frostspirit Kai has been long due for. Her viability against Starred Aliens has always been dubious at best, but this ability facilitates an entirely new set of matchups into Shibalien Elite, Star Peng, Mesocosmocyclone, Project A., Corporal Weyland, Commander Ostromeda, and even Techn-Old Hyena depending on the situation. For a cheap immunity, this can be easily worth your NP if you find yourself using Frostspirit Kai regularly.

'''HP Buff''' is obviously a very good Talent on a tanker, so there's not much of a need to elaborate on that front. '''Attack Buff''' doesn't do much; Frostspirit Kai is not particularly geared towards damage.

